      "doc": {
        "why": "GBA response, NSO color matrix, luminance, then the cgwg subpixel grid so the panel reads as an AGB-001 LCD",
        "passes": "Colour passes stay at the native 240x160, unfiltered, and only the grid renders at the viewport: lcd-grid-v2 takes its LCD cell from its source size, so a viewport-sized source turns one cell into one screen pixel (no grid, flat lifted blacks, 1-px subpixel streaks). This is the upstream nds/3ds-lcd-grid-v2 structure.",
        "params": "The same grid as gbc/screen.slangp, tuned on settled frames: luminance 1.0 keeps the image-adjustment pass from clipping HSV value (1.4 flattened every grey from 187 up in a running game), gamma 1.2 with black level 0.02 follows round two's one-frame tone curve, subpixels leaking 0.5 with gain 1.3 give a white of about 228 with under half of any channel at 255 (gain 1.8 put 72/60/52% there), red and green subpixels 0.96 and blue 0.83 keep it warm, and saturation 2.6 pays back the leak. blacklevel and ambient 0 take the lift off black (54 before)."
