      "doc": {
        "why": "PSP colour profile, then the lcd3x grid. lcd1x_psp's -0.25 phase puts both samples of a 2x pixel on sine zeros, so the Deck's 2x lane showed no grid at all; lcd3x's one-sided phase draws the gap at every integer scale from 2x up.",
        "params": "brighten_scanlines 12.5 gives a 15% row gap; brighten_lcd 7.7 gives a 20% subpixel swing at 2x."
      },
      "output": {
        "sha256": "64d49dd29a0e02fda7a02f1ae62d934e6b4f7e60a80cfd904d778b42c413b8cf"
